    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91290.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, we were always concerned if it was close, because we all remember 2020 when it looked like President Trump was winning. We all kind of get late at night, and then everything changes the next morning. So I was hoping it was going to be, as President Trump said, throughout the campaign, too big to rig. And that's exactly what happened. It was overwhelming for him. It brought Senators Bernie Marino won our state. I mean, be sure around the five, six points. So it was all because of President Trump. And what I really think happened, frankly, Joe, is the American people said, we're tired of being called racist, we're tired of being called deplorable, we're tired of being called garbage, and we're tired of an economy that stinks in an open border. And they said, we're going to send a message loud and clear, and they did across the board. But it would not have happened but for the perseverance and the leadership and the toughness of President Trump.",
